# Read Email — auto on new case (no typed RE in normal flow)

**Chat scope:** Email processing chat only (`EMAIL-PROCESSING-AGENT.md`).

**Operator does NOT type RE** to receive the 7-step RE or Auto-LF. The agent runs the full EMAIL pipeline **automatically** as soon as a new case is detected.

**Always stick to the processing form:** Full 7-step output from **sprinklr-read-answer-email** SKILL.md.

### Auto-trigger (normal workday — no RE command)

| Trigger | Agent action (EMAIL) |
|---------|----------------------|
| **EMAIL sidetray click** (`CASE_ITEM_AUTO_CLICKED` → `SIDETRAY_EMAIL_PROCESSING_IMMEDIATE`) | Script **immediately** opens case + extract — **zero operator input** |
| **`--await-arm` extract** completes (`DETACHED_ARM_EXTRACT_READY` / `CUSTOMER EMAIL` + `RE_TEXT_ONLY_GATE`) | Agent **same workflow** immediately continues three-turn RE → Auto-LF → wait **PR** or transfer arm — **no new user message, no typed RE** |
| **First case after login** — case visible in Sprinklr | Agent auto-runs `run.py --once` (consumes `FIRST_RE_ONCE_PENDING`) — **do not wait for typed RE** |
| **CALL** (`CHANNEL: CALL` / `CALL_LF_GATE`) | Auto-LF voice + close-out arm — no 7-step, no PR unless asked |

**Typed RE / `run.py --once`** = **recovery only** (re-read visible case, `--await-arm` failed, manual refresh). Not the operator’s normal command.

### HARD BAN — never skip the 7-step RE (EMAIL)

For every **CHANNEL: EMAIL** case (auto extract after login, `--await-arm`, or recovery `--once`):

1. You **MUST** write the full **7-step RE as visible chat text** (plain assistant message the user can read without opening any UI menu).  
2. **Forbidden shortcuts:** Auto-LF only; “transfer done” one-liner; paste-ready reply without sections 1–5/7; tool-only turn with no 7-step text.  
3. **Forbidden hiding:** Do **not** put the 7-step only inside tool results, background-task panels, collapsed **“finished N background tasks”** / task dropdowns, or anything the user must click to expand. The 7-step must appear as **normal chat prose** above the fold.  
4. **Turn order (EMAIL):**  
   - Extract (`run.py` / await-arm) may use tools first.  
   - **Next:** sections **1–7 as plain chat text** — **text-only assistant message** strongly preferred (no Task/subagent, no parallel tool batch before prose). See `.cursor/rules/re-no-background-tasks-ui.mdc`.  
   - **Only after** that visible text: `--play-ready`, **Auto-LF**, transfer arm **or** wait for **PR**.  
   - Operator recovery: **`RE SHOW`** / **`visible RE`** → re-print full 7-step in main thread; **`RE FILE`** → `show_latest_re.py`.  
5. Transfer-eligible EMAIL still gets all 7 sections visible in chat (section 6 may be short forward notice).  
6. **CALL** does **not** use the email 7-step form (Auto-LF voice on CHANNEL detect).  

If you already ran Auto-LF / tools without a visible 7-step in chat: **STOP**, output the full 7-step as normal chat text for the visible Fall # now, then continue.

**AI model:** Prefer **Claude 4.6 Sonnet** for EMAIL RE. **Grok banned.** See `.cursor/rules/ai-model-stay-auto.mdc`.

## Detached arm (mandatory — why watches used to “die”)

Cursor **aborts** long-running agent shells (~20s) when a turn ends. That used to kill the in-shell Anwenden/Weiter/Extern watch → `ERROR: ANWENDEN WATCH DIED BEFORE EXTRACT` → `--once` recovery.

**Fix:** `--arm` / `--arm-weiter` / `--arm-extern` spawn a **detached** Windows process by default (`ARM_WATCH_DETACHED`). Cursor aborting the shell does **not** kill the listener. Log: `.cursor/state/arm_watch.log`.

| Step | Command | Expect |
|------|---------|--------|
| 1 | `run.py --arm` (or `--arm-weiter` / `--arm-extern`) | `ARM_WATCH_DETACHED` + `READY_FOR_YOUR_CLICK` + Dexter; parent exits; **no console window** |
| 2 | Chat + finishing quote | `Armed — click … now.` + `PR done` / `LF done` / `LF TR done` |
| 3 | `run.py --await-arm` | Poll until extract **or** fail-fast on `ERROR: NEXT CASE NOT OPEN` |
| 3b | **EMAIL sidetray path** | On `CASE_ITEM_AUTO_CLICKED` script runs extract **immediately** in same automation chain — agent must **not** pause for operator input before 7-step |
| 4 | Full **7-step RE** + `--play-ready` + **Auto-LF** | Start **immediately** when await-arm / extract stdout completes — book cue after section 7; then Case Tracker (see `lf-log-form.mdc`) |

- **Click-ready = Dexter + READY_FOR_YOUR_CLICK** — do not wait for await to finish before clicking.
- If **`--await-arm`** is aborted by Cursor → **re-run `--await-arm`** (detached watch still running).
- If log shows **`ERROR: NEXT CASE NOT OPEN`** → **`run.py --once`** on the visible case (arm already stopped).
- Use **`--once`** also if `ARM_WATCH_LOG` has **no** CUSTOMER EMAIL after timeout.
- **Never** start a second `--arm*` while a detached watch is still waiting.
- **`--foreground`** = legacy blocking watch (debug only).

### Next-case click (after Anwenden / Weiter / Weiterleiten)

Script remembers **closed Fall #**, skips that sidebar item, polls ~25s for a different case, retries if still console/same Fall. Hard fail → stop arm + `--once` tip (no second Weiterleiten wait).

## Normal workday (operator never types RE)

1. **login** (once) → Case Tracker tab; agent **auto-extracts** first visible case (`run.py --once`) — no RE prompt.
2. Agent writes full **7-step RE** + **Auto-LF** automatically.
3. Non-transfer → operator **PR** only → agent arms Anwenden + **`--await-arm`**.
4. Operator clicks Anwenden / Weiter / Extern / Next → **`--await-arm`** extract → agent **auto** 7-step + Auto-LF again (no RE).
5. Repeat until **DONE**.

**Operator types in normal flow:** **login**, **PR**, close-out clicks, **DONE** — not **RE**, not **LF**.

## Recovery — when user sends **RE** / **re** / **RE SHOW** / **RE FILE**

**Hard rule:** Typed **RE** = **manual re-extract** (`--once`) or visibility recovery — **not** the default path. It must **never** arm Anwenden.

1. Run default RE entrypoint:
   ```powershell
   Set-Location "c:\Users\PC ENTER\Desktop\Citrix"; uv run python .cursor/skills/sprinklr-read-answer-email/run.py
   ```
   Expect **`MODE: --once`** and either `FIRST_RE_ONCE_CONSUMED` (after login) or `RE_ONCE_DEFAULT`. **Trust script stdout:** `CHANNEL: CALL` + `CALL_LF_GATE` → voice Auto-LF + Next (no 7-step). `CHANNEL: EMAIL` + `CUSTOMER EMAIL` + `RE_TEXT_ONLY_GATE` → three-turn 7-step RE (see `sprinklr-call-vs-email.mdc`).
2. **Do not** run `--arm` / `--await-arm` on typed RE. Arms run after Auto-LF / PR close-out (below).
3. **Audio:**
   - **Armed auto-RE start:** After Anwenden / Weiter / Extern / Next → sidetray poll (`SIDETRAY_WATCH_ARMED`) → **EMAIL:** click sidetray item; **CALL:** skip click, wait for overlay (`SIDETRAY_CALL_AUTO_OPEN`) → extract begins → Prowler (`ARMED_RE_START_SOUND`).
   - **RE ready (after section 7):** Hook plays book-opening cue (`RE_READY_SOUND`) when `RE_PENDING_SOUND` was set — case is ready to read.
   - **PR done / LF TR done:** Finishing quotes → Dexter (`PR_LF_DONE_SOUND`).
   - Manual: **`sound`** → `--play-ready`.
4. After 7-step + `--play-ready`: **Auto-LF** (do not wait for typed `LF`). See `.cursor/rules/lf-log-form.mdc`.
5. **EMAIL non-transfer:** wait for user **PR** → after paste succeeds → **`--arm`** + **`--await-arm`**. Finishing quote `PR done for #FALL_ID`.
6. **EMAIL / CALL transfer:** after Auto-LF Transfer Ja → **`--arm-weiter`** or **`--arm-extern`** + await. Quote `LF TR done for #FALL_ID`.
7. **CALL:** on CHANNEL detect → **immediately Auto-LF** voice → **`--arm-next`** (or transfer arm) + await. Quote `LF done for #FALL_ID`. Do **not** wait for BRIEF.

### Explicit modes

| Command | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| `run.py` / typed **RE** | **Recovery `--once`** — re-read visible case (not normal flow) |
| `run.py --once` | Same (explicit recovery) |
| `run.py --arm` | Arm Anwenden (**detached**; after **PR** on EMAIL non-transfer) |
| `run.py --arm-weiter` | Arm Weiter (**detached**; after transfer Auto-LF / LF TR **queue**) |
| `run.py --arm-extern` | Arm Extern (**detached**; after transfer Auto-LF / LF TR **email**) |
| `run.py --arm-next` | Arm call disposition **Next** (**detached**; after **CALL** Auto-LF) |
| `run.py --await-arm` | Poll `arm_watch.log` until extract done |
| `run.py --foreground` | Debug only: blocking in-shell watch |

## After extract: 7-step + Auto-LF (mandatory)

Every EMAIL extract (auto after login, `--await-arm`, or recovery `--once`):

1. Full **7-step RE as visible chat text** (sections 1–7 — user must see it without expanding “finished background tasks” / any dropdown)  
2. **Only then** **`re_complete_sound.py --play-ready`**  
3. **Only then** **Auto-LF** for this Fall # (Transfer Nein or Ja per §3) — user does **not** type `LF`  
4. If Auto-LF prints **`PAUSE_AUTO_LF`** + **`LF_CONTINUE_AFTER_SPEICHERN_ARMED`** (exit `3`): warn user to click Speichern for the **previous** LF; Auto-LF for the **current** Fall # continues automatically — run **`fill_case_tracker.py --await-speichern-continue`**, then on **`CONTINUE_LF_DONE`** do transfer arm or wait for **PR**. Do **not** require a manual Auto-LF retry after Speichern.  
5. If transfer → arm Weiter/Extern immediately; if non-transfer → stop and wait for **PR**

**Auto-LF / tool runs must never replace, precede, or hide the 7-step behind Cursor task UI.**

Every CALL on CHANNEL detect: Auto-LF `--channel voice` → arm Next (or Weiter/Extern if transfer). BRIEF is optional and never blocks Auto-LF.

## Auto-arm after **PR** (EMAIL non-transfer / Anwenden)

LF was already done at RE time. When user sends **PR** / **pr** and paste + verify succeed:

1. **Immediately** arm Anwenden (detached):
   ```powershell
   Set-Location "c:\Users\PC ENTER\Desktop\Citrix"; uv run python .cursor/skills/sprinklr-read-answer-email/run.py --arm
   ```
   Expect **`ANWENDEN_RE_ARMED`** + **`ARM_WATCH_DETACHED`** + **`READY_FOR_YOUR_CLICK: Anwenden`**.
2. Chat: `Armed — click Anwenden now.` + `PR done for #FALL_ID` (or `PR LF done` if manual PR LF path).
3. Then **`--await-arm`** → next case → agent **auto** 7-step + Auto-LF (operator does **not** type RE).

**Do not** arm Anwenden at Auto-LF time for non-transfer EMAIL (wait for PR).

### Auto-arm after **CALL** Auto-LF — disposition **Next**

After Auto-LF `--channel voice` succeeds:

1. **`--arm-next`** (not Anwenden) → Dexter → `LF done for #FALL_ID` → **`--await-arm`**  
2. User clicks exact **Next**. After extract: CHANNEL again → process + Auto-LF.

| Trigger | Arm when | Arm script | Then |
|---------|----------|------------|------|
| **PR** (EMAIL non-transfer; Auto-LF already done) | After PR paste+verify | **`--arm`** | **`--await-arm`** |
| **Auto-LF / LF TR** (transfer queue) | After transfer fill | **`--arm-weiter`** | **`--await-arm`** |
| **Auto-LF / LF TR** (transfer email) | After transfer fill | **`--arm-extern`** | **`--await-arm`** |
| **Auto-LF** (CALL voice) | After voice fill | **`--arm-next`** | **`--await-arm`** |
| Manual **PR LF** (recovery) | After PR + LF | **`--arm`** | **`--await-arm`** |

Do **not** arm twice for the same close-out. If a detached watch is already waiting, do not start a second overlapping arm.

## 7-step output

**Language:** Sections **1–5** and **7** → **English** (to the operator). Section **6** → **German only** (customer). All other agent chat to the user → English. See `.cursor/rules/agent-english-user-customer-german.mdc`.

1. Customer summary (EN)  
2. Verification (EN)  
3. Transfer eligibility (EN)  
4a/4b. Backend / instructions (EN)  
5. Instructions on handling case (EN)  
6. Your response to customer (**German**, code block; **chat** soft-wrap ~72 for vertical read; **PR** uses mail-format length — not chat wraps)  
7. Summary of response (EN) — then run **`re_complete_sound.py --play-ready`** (book) — then **Auto-LF**

## Integrity

- One visible case only; discard prior Fall # context on each new **RE**.
- PR pastes latest RE for the **same visible Fall #** only.
- Watch loop must **not** steal browser focus (`bring_to_front`) while waiting.
- **No monitor fallback:** If Anwenden-gated RE fails, **stop and report**. Do **not** fall into continuous `monitor_emails` / `get_new_emails` loops.

## Rollback

If this experiment fails or you dislike it, in the **instructions** chat type **`revert last`** — restores checkpoint `.cursor/revert-checkpoints/pre-anwenden-re/`.

## Hooks note

Requires project hooks enabled (`.cursor/hooks.json`). View **Output → Hooks** if sound does not play.
